<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  RUT_TradeMootDroids.xml       RimUtinni Patches · DROID_FACTION_LOADOUTS_1
                                (packet C1), authored 2026-09-08
  ============================================================================

  Builds the Jawa Trade Moot row of DROID_UNIFIED_FRAMEWORK_DESIGN.md §3.2:
  "buys/sells droids of all kinds, and brain parts | StockGenerator_Colonists
  on DW kinds; brain-trio stock, rare" — under owner ruling 2, verbatim: "the
  Trade Moot loves droids of all kinds and buys/sells them, just like you."

  These three TraderKindDefs are appended to `Jawa_IndigenousTribes`'s
  `caravanTraderKinds` and `baseTraderKinds` in
  Defs/FactionDefs/JawaTribes.xml. They do NOT replace TribeBase's own
  Caravan_Neolithic_* / Base_Neolithic_Standard entries — RimWorld appends a
  child's list to the parent's, so these are extra rolls beside the ordinary
  tribal traders, which is why their commonalities are below 1.

  🔴 THE GENERATOR CLASS IS OURS, AND THE FIRST TRY WAS WRONG IN A WAY WORTH
  RECORDING. §3.2 names `StockGenerator_Colonists`; that is an EXAMPLE, and it
  turned out to belong to a mod this program retires. Every off-the-shelf route
  was measured against the live 600-mod set and every one of them fails:

      StockGenerator_Colonists    17 uses, ALL guy762.mm.kotorcore — §2's R4
                                  retires that mod. There is no vanilla class of
                                  this name.
      StockGenerator_Automatons    9 uses. Its real name is
                                  `Asimov.StockGenerator_Automatons` and its own
                                  donor gates it on Neronix17.OuterRim.DroidDepot,
                                  NOT on Outer Rim Core (measured in the donor's
                                  TraderKinds_Base.xml:83) — so §2's R3 kills it,
                                  before D4 has even run.
      StockGenerator_Slaves      vanilla, and silently inert:
                                  StockGenerator_Slaves.cs lines 20-35 yield
                                  NOTHING unless every ideo of the trading faction
                                  returns IdeoApprovesOfSlavery(), and the Moot's
                                  fixedIdeo is The Salvation.

  🔴 THE FIRST BUILD OF THIS FILE SHIPPED `Class="StockGenerator_Automatons"`
  WITHOUT THE `Asimov.` NAMESPACE AND BOTH DEFS WERE DISCARDED — the 2026-09-08
  20:26 full-list load logged "Could not find type named
  StockGenerator_Automatons" twice and then two dangling
  caravanTraderKinds/baseTraderKinds cross-references, because the faction's <li>
  survives a def that does not. The short-name `$type` in a def DUMP is not the
  `Class=` string; the dump prints the type's name, the loader wants a name
  GenTypes can resolve. Do not read one as the other.

  ⇒ `RimMandrake.StarWars.Droidworks.StockGenerator_DWDroids`, written for this
  (Source/Droidworks/StockGenerator_DWDroids.cs). It outlives R1-R4, it has no
  slavery gate — a droid is property, not a person — and its HandlesThingDef keys
  on RSW_DW_FleshType_Droid, so the Moot BUYS any Droidworks droid the player
  brings, not only the models it is selling today. That is the "buys" half of
  ruling 2, and with a third-party class it was unprovable.

  ⚠️ EVERY DEF HERE CARRIES `MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.droidworks"` ON ITS ROOT
  ELEMENT, and the identical string is on the faction's own
  caravanTraderKinds/baseTraderKinds <li> in JawaTribes.xml. Both halves are
  needed: a `Class=` naming a type no loaded assembly has discards the whole def
  (memory: modextension-missing-type-discards-def), and a faction that still
  lists a discarded def logs a dangling cross-reference. That pairing is what the
  first build got wrong.

  🔴 THE DLL AND THIS FILE SHIP TOGETHER OR NOT AT ALL. StockGenerator_DWDroids
  lives in Droidworks.dll, and an assembly can only be replaced while the game is
  CLOSED. Deploying this XML against an older DLL reproduces exactly the discard
  above. Same rule the Inhabited cast rosters were held under in DEPLOY_HOLD.txt.

  ⚠️ Bought droids arrive UNBOLTED, deliberately. RSW_DW_BoltResentment is seeded
  by the two APPLICATION routes (Recipe_InstallRestrainingBolt.ApplyOnPawn /
  JobDriver_DWClampBolt's AddFinishAction), never by a hediff merely appearing on
  a pawn — so a droid bolted by a stock generator would carry a bolt that never
  earns resentment and never rebels when freed, which is half a mechanism wearing
  the whole one's face. Selling bolted droids belongs with B5's payoff.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       1 · The parts caravan. No third-party class, so it survives every
       retirement wave in §2 — which matters, because ruling 6's head-gate
       economy ("you import them... nobody on this world can, or ever will")
       has no other supply route than salvage, quest loot and this.
       countRange 0~2 per part IS the "rare" of §3.2: a caravan can and often
       will arrive carrying none of the three.
       ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <TraderKindDef MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.droidworks">
    <defName>RUT_Caravan_TradeMoot_DroidParts</defName>
    <label>droid parts trader</label>
    <commonality>0.5</commonality>
    <requestable>true</requestable>
    <orbital>false</orbital>
    <stockGenerators>

      <li Class="StockGenerator_SingleDef">
        <thingDef>Silver</thingDef>
        <countRange>1500~4000</countRange>
      </li>

      <!-- SELL: the brain trio, rare. -->
      <li Class="StockGenerator_SingleDef">
        <thingDef>RSW_DW_PersonalityMatrix</thingDef>
        <countRange>0~2</countRange>
      </li>
      <li Class="StockGenerator_SingleDef">
        <thingDef>RSW_DW_Processor</thingDef>
        <countRange>0~2</countRange>
      </li>
      <li Class="StockGenerator_SingleDef">
        <thingDef>RSW_DW_Databank</thingDef>
        <countRange>0~2</countRange>
      </li>

      <!-- BUY: "and brain parts" cuts both ways. A Jawa strips a wreck and
           sells the head; this is where that head turns into silver. -->
      <li Class="StockGenerator_BuySingleDef">
        <thingDef>RSW_DW_PersonalityMatrix</thingDef>
      </li>
      <li Class="StockGenerator_BuySingleDef">
        <thingDef>RSW_DW_Processor</thingDef>
      </li>
      <li Class="StockGenerator_BuySingleDef">
        <thingDef>RSW_DW_Databank</thingDef>
      </li>

      <li Class="StockGenerator_BuyExpensiveSimple" />

    </stockGenerators>
  </TraderKindDef>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       2 · The droid caravan. "Droids of all kinds" is taken literally: one
       generator for the ordinary working chassis a market actually moves,
       and a second, much thinner one for military hulls.
       ⛔ Every kind listed is a *_Colonist / *_Good build. Droidworks ships a
       raider-grade "Bad" variant of the same chassis at 125-500 combatPower;
       those are what the Empire and the Junkers field, not what anyone sells
       over a counter, and putting them on a market would hand the player an
       HK-50 for silver.
       ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <TraderKindDef MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.droidworks">
    <defName>RUT_Caravan_TradeMoot_Droids</defName>
    <label>droid trader</label>
    <commonality>0.5</commonality>
    <requestable>true</requestable>
    <orbital>false</orbital>
    <stockGenerators>

      <li Class="StockGenerator_SingleDef">
        <thingDef>Silver</thingDef>
        <countRange>2000~5000</countRange>
      </li>

      <li Class="RimMandrake.StarWars.Droidworks.StockGenerator_DWDroids">
        <countRange>2~5</countRange>
        <pawnKinds>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_GE3LD</li>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_GE3PD</li>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_KM1MD</li>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_KM1HMD</li>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_R8009UD</li>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_3CUD</li>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_T3UD</li>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_KX12UPD</li>
          <li>RSW_DW_OuterRim_ProtocolDroid</li>
        </pawnKinds>
      </li>

      <!-- The military shelf: 0~1, because a Moot caravan is a market stall,
           not an arms fair. -->
      <li Class="RimMandrake.StarWars.Droidworks.StockGenerator_DWDroids">
        <countRange>0~1</countRange>
        <pawnKinds>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_SentWD</li>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_ADMkI</li>
        </pawnKinds>
      </li>

      <li Class="StockGenerator_SingleDef">
        <thingDef>RSW_DW_PersonalityMatrix</thingDef>
        <countRange>0~2</countRange>
      </li>
      <li Class="StockGenerator_SingleDef">
        <thingDef>RSW_DW_Processor</thingDef>
        <countRange>0~2</countRange>
      </li>
      <li Class="StockGenerator_SingleDef">
        <thingDef>RSW_DW_Databank</thingDef>
        <countRange>0~2</countRange>
      </li>

      <li Class="StockGenerator_BuySingleDef">
        <thingDef>RSW_DW_PersonalityMatrix</thingDef>
      </li>
      <li Class="StockGenerator_BuySingleDef">
        <thingDef>RSW_DW_Processor</thingDef>
      </li>
      <li Class="StockGenerator_BuySingleDef">
        <thingDef>RSW_DW_Databank</thingDef>
      </li>

    </stockGenerators>
  </TraderKindDef>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       3 · The Moot's own settlement market. Same stock, deeper, because this
       is the one a player travels to on purpose — §3.2's "buys/sells droids
       of all kinds" is a place as much as an event. commonality 0.6 against
       TribeBase's single Base_Neolithic_Standard at 1, so roughly a third of
       visits find the droid market rather than the pemmican one.
       ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <TraderKindDef MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.droidworks">
    <defName>RUT_Base_TradeMoot_Droids</defName>
    <label>droid market</label>
    <commonality>0.6</commonality>
    <requestable>false</requestable>
    <orbital>false</orbital>
    <stockGenerators>

      <li Class="StockGenerator_SingleDef">
        <thingDef>Silver</thingDef>
        <countRange>3000~7000</countRange>
      </li>

      <li Class="RimMandrake.StarWars.Droidworks.StockGenerator_DWDroids">
        <countRange>4~8</countRange>
        <pawnKinds>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_GE3LD</li>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_GE3PD</li>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_KM1MD</li>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_KM1HMD</li>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_R8009UD</li>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_3CUD</li>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_T3UD</li>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_KX12UPD</li>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidGood_3C</li>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidGood_R8009</li>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidGood_KX12UPD</li>
          <li>RSW_DW_OuterRim_ProtocolDroid</li>
        </pawnKinds>
      </li>

      <li Class="RimMandrake.StarWars.Droidworks.StockGenerator_DWDroids">
        <countRange>0~2</countRange>
        <pawnKinds>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_SentWD</li>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_ADMkI</li>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_ADMkIV</li>
        </pawnKinds>
      </li>

      <li Class="StockGenerator_SingleDef">
        <thingDef>RSW_DW_PersonalityMatrix</thingDef>
        <countRange>1~3</countRange>
      </li>
      <li Class="StockGenerator_SingleDef">
        <thingDef>RSW_DW_Processor</thingDef>
        <countRange>1~3</countRange>
      </li>
      <li Class="StockGenerator_SingleDef">
        <thingDef>RSW_DW_Databank</thingDef>
        <countRange>1~3</countRange>
      </li>

      <li Class="StockGenerator_BuySingleDef">
        <thingDef>RSW_DW_PersonalityMatrix</thingDef>
      </li>
      <li Class="StockGenerator_BuySingleDef">
        <thingDef>RSW_DW_Processor</thingDef>
      </li>
      <li Class="StockGenerator_BuySingleDef">
        <thingDef>RSW_DW_Databank</thingDef>
      </li>

      <li Class="StockGenerator_BuyExpensiveSimple" />

    </stockGenerators>
  </TraderKindDef>

</Defs>
